From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:14:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 08/79] flashnext_mia: lane backend and native family for
 serving

Her engine behind the native server's lane core: the lane backend (cuda_lanes.zig) with shared forwards over
up to --parallel streams, prompts filled in layer slices between rounds and bursts of prompts in one pass,
kept prompt states for the prompt cache, the MTP head's own chain stops and joined streams' first drafts in
one batch; and the family the server opens (cuda_native.zig): options, the two ranks' link, settings
agreement and NCCL, the mirror on rank 0 and the follower loop on rank 1.

Source: patches/0007-serving.patch @ MiaAI-Lab/Qwen3.8-Flash-Dual-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold dc05c912342e
Port: zig/src/families/flashnext/cuda_{lanes,native}.zig moved to zig/src/families/flashnext_mia/; paths naming her moved files rewritten.
Port: her lane core and lane host hunks are not applied; f212 provides each capability with its own interface, which her backend must adopt in the compile step:
Port: - fills between rounds (backend prefill_begin + prefill_step(streams, FillState[]), Engine.fill_hook/beginStream/fillingCount, LaneHost filled/startOne, fake backendSliced and their tests): f212's prefill_step(s, max_rows) bool, cancel_prefill and lane_host_fill.zig;
Port: - prompt bursts (prefill_many returning error.BurstRefused, Engine.prefillBurst/addPrefilled, LaneHost admitAll/startBurst): f212's prefill_many -> bool with many_rows (lane_host_admit.zig, lanes/open.zig);
Port: - head-stopped chains (Model.draft_stops, Rule.head_stops/stopsNow): f212's draft_confidence (a greedy stream asks the most drafts, chains cut by the head's chances); her draft_stops_most live-stream cap has no f212 counterpart and is not ported;
Port: - joined streams' first drafts in one batch (Model.join_batch, Engine.joinDrafts, Stream.join_draft): f212's join_drafts with join_tail;
Port: - image and video rows (lanes.Media, Stream/Request.media, never kept or resumed): f212's Request.images and Info.vision; this engine is refused --vision until it reads them;
Port: - tool_choice call gates (core/lanes/call_gate.zig, Stream.gate, Engine.correctCall and the commit cut): dropped with the server half in 0001, f212 enforces required calls with tool_grammar structures.
